# Data Profiling and Visualization Utilities

A Python module providing a comprehensive suite of functions for **exploratory data analysis (EDA)**, **feature distribution visualization**, **outlier detection**, and **target analysis**. Supports both **categorical/discrete** and **continuous/numeric** variables and includes utilities for handling **missing values and sentinel values**.  

All functions are defined in the script: `credit_risk_feature_engineering.py`.

---

## Features

### 1. Missing Value Analysis
- `check_missing_values(df: pd.DataFrame, missing_value_rules: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> pd.DataFrame`  
  - Checks standard NA values and optional **sentinel values**.  
  - Returns a DataFrame summarizing **missing counts** and **percentages**.  
  - Example sentinel values: `{"fico_score": 99999, "income": -1, "inq_last_6m": 99}`  

---

### 2. Distribution Plots

#### Discrete / Categorical
- `plot_discrete_distribution(df, col, missing_sentinel=None, title=None, palette="viridis", figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Bar chart with **missing values as a separate category**.  

- `plot_channel_distribution(df, channel_col="channel", title="Loan Channel Distribution", palette="viridis", figsize=(10,6))`  
  - Plots loan channels with **percentages annotated**.  

- `plot_product_type_distribution(df, product_col="product_type", title="Product Type Distribution", palette="rocket", figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Handles missing values; visualizes product types.  

- `plot_state_distribution(df, state_col="state", title="Distribution of Loans by State", palette="coolwarm", figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Plots state-wise distribution with missing values if any.  

#### Continuous / Numeric
- `plot_continuous_distribution_hist(df, col, title=None, color="skyblue", bins=30, figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Histogram with **KDE** and a **stats box** (mean, median, std, missing).  

- `plot_float_distribution_hist(df, col, missing_sentinel=-1.0, title="Distribution Plot", color="skyblue", figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Similar to above but allows **custom missing sentinel**.  

#### Special Variables
- `plot_fico_score_distribution(df, fico_col="fico_score", missing_sentinel=99999, title="FICO Score Distribution", palette="Blues_d", figsize=(10,5))`  
  - Bins FICO scores into **standard credit ranges**; missing sentinel handled.  

- `plot_income_distribution(df, income_col="income", missing_sentinel=-1, title="Income Distribution", palette="Blues_d", figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Predefined **income ranges**; missing sentinel handled.  

- `plot_employment_length_distribution(df, emp_col="employment_length", missing_sentinel=-1, title="Employment Length Distribution", palette="Greens_d", figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Predefined employment buckets; missing sentinel handled.  

- `plot_age_distribution(df, age_col="age", missing_sentinel=-1, title="Age Distribution", palette="Purples_d", figsize=(12,6))`  
  - Predefined age groups; missing sentinel handled.  

---

### 3. Outlier Detection and Visualization
- `detect_outliers_iqr(df, col, lower_percentile=0.25, upper_percentile=0.75, multiplier=1.5) -> dict`  
  - Detects outliers using **IQR method**.  
  - Automatically **handles sentinel values** for FICO, inquiries, and income.  
  - Returns counts, percentages, bounds, and min/max values.  

- `plot_outlier_boxplot(df, col, figsize=(8,6))`  
  - Visualizes outliers with **missing values annotated**.  

---

### 4. Target Analysis
- `plot_default_rate_by_feature(df, feature_col, target_col="default_12m", title=None, figsize=(12,6), top_n=None, include_missing=True)`  
  - Plots **default rate by feature levels** with sample sizes.  
  - Includes **missing values** as a separate category.  
  - Can limit to **top N categories**.  
  - Uses **dual axes**: bars for default rate, line for counts.  

